.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 

.SH "Retry utility"
.PP
by \fRNicholas C\&. Zakas\fP

.PP
If you find this useful, please consider supporting my work with a \fRdonation\fP or \fRnominate me\fP for a GitHub Star\&.
.SH "Description"
.PP
A utility for retrying failed async JavaScript calls based on the error returned\&.
.SH "Usage"
.PP
.SS "Node\&.js"
Install using \fRnpm\fP or \fRyarn\fP:

.PP
.PP
.nf
npm install @humanwhocodes/retry

# or

yarn add @humanwhocodes/retry
.fi
.PP

.PP
Import into your Node\&.js project:

.PP
.PP
.nf
// CommonJS
const { Retrier } = require("@humanwhocodes/retry");

// ESM
import { Retrier } from "@humanwhocodes/retry";
.fi
.PP
.SS "Deno"
Install using \fRJSR\fP:

.PP
.PP
.nf
deno add @humanwhocodes/retry

#or

jsr add @humanwhocodes/retry
.fi
.PP

.PP
Then import into your Deno project:

.PP
.PP
.nf
import { Retrier } from "@humanwhocodes/retry";
.fi
.PP
.SS "Bun"
Install using this command:

.PP
.PP
.nf
bun add @humanwhocodes/retry
.fi
.PP

.PP
Import into your Bun project:

.PP
.PP
.nf
import { Retrier } from "@humanwhocodes/retry";
.fi
.PP
.SS "Browser"
It's recommended to import the minified version to save bandwidth:

.PP
.PP
.nf
import { Retrier } from "https://cdn\&.skypack\&.dev/@humanwhocodes/retry?min";
.fi
.PP

.PP
However, you can also import the unminified version for debugging purposes:

.PP
.PP
.nf
import { Retrier } from "https://cdn\&.skypack\&.dev/@humanwhocodes/retry";
.fi
.PP
.SH "API"
.PP
After importing, create a new instance of \fRRetrier\fP and specify the function to run on the error\&. This function should return \fRtrue\fP if you want the call retried and \fRfalse\fP if not\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
// this instance will retry if the specific error code is found
const retrier = new Retrier(error => {
    return error\&.code === "ENFILE" || error\&.code === "EMFILE";
});
.fi
.PP

.PP
Then, call the \fRretry()\fP method around the function you'd like to retry, such as:

.PP
.PP
.nf
import fs from "fs/promises";

const retrier = new Retrier(error => {
    return error\&.code === "ENFILE" || error\&.code === "EMFILE";
});

const text = await retrier\&.retry(() => fs\&.readFile("README\&.md", "utf8"));
.fi
.PP

.PP
The \fRretry()\fP method will either pass through the result on success or wait and retry on failure\&. Any error that isn't caught by the retrier is automatically rejected so the end result is a transparent passing through of both success and failure\&.
.SS "Setting a Timeout"
You can control how long a task will attempt to retry before giving up by passing the \fRtimeout\fP option to the \fRRetrier\fP constructor\&. By default, the timeout is one minute\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
import fs from "fs/promises";

const retrier = new Retrier(error => {
    return error\&.code === "ENFILE" || error\&.code === "EMFILE";
}, { timeout: 100_000 });

const text = await retrier\&.retry(() => fs\&.readFile("README\&.md", "utf8"));
.fi
.PP

.PP
When a call times out, it rejects the first error that was received from calling the function\&.
.SS "Setting a Concurrency Limit"
When processing a large number of function calls, you can limit the number of concurrent function calls by passing the \fRconcurrency\fP option to the \fRRetrier\fP constructor\&. By default, \fRconcurrency\fP is 1000\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
import fs from "fs/promises";

const retrier = new Retrier(error => {
    return error\&.code === "ENFILE" || error\&.code === "EMFILE";
}, { concurrency: 100 });

const filenames = getFilenames();
const contents = await Promise\&.all(
    filenames\&.map(filename => retrier\&.retry(() => fs\&.readFile(filename, "utf8"))
);
.fi
.PP
.SS "Aborting with \fRAbortSignal\fP"
You can also pass an \fRAbortSignal\fP to cancel a retry:

.PP
.PP
.nf
import fs from "fs/promises";

const controller = new AbortController();
const retrier = new Retrier(error => {
    return error\&.code === "ENFILE" || error\&.code === "EMFILE";
});

const text = await retrier\&.retry(
    () => fs\&.readFile("README\&.md", "utf8"),
    { signal: controller\&.signal }
);
.fi
.PP
